        annotations:
        - name: annotate1
          mode: annotate
          title: Gaia MQTT Ingest -- Canvas / Brain State / Dream
          text: 'Subscribes gaia/td/canvas, gaia/brain/state, gaia/brain/dream and caches the raw JSON per topic. Derived Script CHOP/DAT outputs: soul mood (out_soul), top-20 lexicon words + rotating current word, latest LLM thought. Gated by Services > Canvas Ingest (logic-level gate -- the mqttclientDAT connection itself always stays up).'
          position: [-70, -290]
          size: [1870, 1250]
          color: [0.325, 0.5, 0.3]
        - name: annotate2
          mode: annotate
          title: Direct Mocap Ingest (OSC)
          text: Receives face/hand/pose/meta landmarks via OSC (port = Mocapport, default 7000) from a Gaia OPS node's mediapipe_node.py, scoped to /gaia/mocap/{Opsdevice}/*. Bounded, deterministic-slice extraction per channel family (unstable/unbounded raw addressing, no automatic expiry). Gated by Services > Direct Mocap Ingest, which binds oscin_mocap's own Active parameter directly (safe -- this is a CHOP, not a mqttclientDAT). Running 2+ gaia_client instances in one project (e.g. one per rig)? Give each a distinct Mocapport if more than one has mocap ingest enabled.
          position: [-70, -2390]
          size: [1070, 1650]
          color: [0.3, 0.45, 0.55]
        - name: annotate3
          mode: annotate
          title: Device Registration (this instance as a controllable device)
          text: 'Publishes gaia/device/{id}/status heartbeat + gaia/devices/{id}/announce+profile, and accepts remote enable/disable/restart/set commands. Register real controls per-project via gaia_device_agent.module.register_service()/register_param() -- see its docstring. Gated by Services > Device Status (logic-level -- connection always stays up). WARNING: device_id defaults to td-{hostname}; do not run two Gaia device agents with the same device_id in the same project/network at once (they will fight over the same MQTT topic). reregister_watch fires the Services > Re-register pulse into gaia_device_agent.reregister() (GAIA_INTERFACE.md section 2) -- retries whatever project registrar was set via register_project_registrar() without restarting TD.'
          position: [-70, -3390]
          size: [1470, 450]
          color: [0.55, 0.45, 0.3]
        - name: annotate4
          mode: annotate
          title: Device Fleet Control + Broker Auto-Discovery
          text: 'Fleet control: subscribes gaia/device/+/status for ALL Gaia devices, maintains devices_table, exposes gaia_fleet_control.send_command(device_id, service, action). Gated by Services > Device Fleet Control. Beacon discovery: probes UDP 8899 every 30s to self-correct Brokerhost if it drifts; gated by Services > Broker Auto-Discovery (off by default). No bundled UI -- bind a List COMP to devices_table per-project.'
          position: [-70, -4890]
          size: [1070, 950]
          color: [0.5, 0.35, 0.5]
        - name: annotate5
          mode: annotate
          title: Portable Export
          text: 'pre_release hook (Embody ExportPortableTox): blanks instance/project identity pars (Deviceid, Family, Stanza, opshortcut, Name) on the staged export copy only -- never touches the live component.'
          position: [-70, -5620]
          size: [270, 330]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
      - name: gaia_config
        type: baseCOMP
        custom_pars:
          Deployment:
          - name: Brokerhost
            style: Str
            label: MQTT Broker Host
            startSection: true
            default: 192.168.1.142
            help: IP o hostname del broker MQTT di Gaia (Core/minipc). UNICO punto da cambiare per portare il progetto su una rete diversa -- mqtt_bridge, gaia_agent e gaia_control leggono tutti da qui.
          - name: Brokerport
            style: Int
            label: MQTT Broker Port
            default: 1883
            min: 1.0
            max: 65535.0
            clampMin: true
            clampMax: true
            help: Porta TCP del broker MQTT di Gaia.
          - name: Corehost
            style: Str
            label: Core Host (OSC out, canale 3)
            startSection: true
            default: 192.168.1.142
            help: IP o hostname del Core/minipc di Gaia per l'OSC out (mood nudge, porta 9008, ricevuto da osc_bridge.py). NON e' l'host di Node-RED/dashboard web -- dal 2026-08-08 quello vive su OPS (192.168.1.240), mentre osc_bridge.py e mosquitto restano su Core. Vedi GAIA_INTERFACE.md 'migrazione Node-RED su OPS'. Coincide oggi con Brokerhost (stessa macchina) e viene aggiornato insieme da beacon_discovery se gaia_beacon risponde.
          - name: Opsdevice
            style: Str
            label: OPS Mocap Device ID
            startSection: true
            default: ops-silvermini2
            help: Device ID pubblicato su MQTT dal nodo OPS (gaia/device/{id}/status) che genera il mocap diretto via OSC (porta 7000, bypassa il Core). Usato per costruire i pattern OSC gaia/mocap/{id}/... in Visuals/mocap_bridge/MocapBridgeExt -- se il nodo OPS ha un id diverso o cambia, aggiorna solo qui.
          - name: Beaconstatus
            style: Str
            label: Beacon Status
            startSection: true
            default: fisso (nessuna risposta dal beacon ancora)
            readOnly: true
            help: 'Ultimo esito della discovery automatica via gaia_beacon (UDP 8899 su Brokerhost, ogni ~30s): ''auto: <ip> (beacon @ ...)'' se ha risposto e Brokerhost/Corehost sono stati aggiornati di conseguenza, altrimenti restano i valori fissi impostati sopra -- nessuna sovrascrittura senza una risposta valida.'
            value: 'auto: 192.168.1.142 (beacon @ core-node-0, 09:42:33)'
        position: [0, -2070]
        size: [160, 130]
        color: [0.325, 0.8, 0.3]
        children:
        - name: beacon_probe
          type: udpoutDAT
          parameters:
            address: =parent().par.Brokerhost.eval()
          position: [1200, 0]
          dat_read_only: true
        - name: camera_resolver
